        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Subtracting Instead of Adding</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">CET is ahead of GMT. You must add 1 hour to GMT. Subtracting 1 hour yields UTC-1, which is incorrect.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Missing Next-Day Rollover</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">23:00 GMT advances to midnight (00:00 CET) on the next day. Always verify the calendar date.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing CET with CEST</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">CET is UTC+1 (winter standard). CEST is UTC+2 (summer daylight saving). Ensure you are converting the active seasonal offset.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing GMT with BST</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">GMT is UTC+0. In summer, the UK shifts to BST (UTC+1). When UK is on BST and Central Europe is on CEST, the difference remains 1 hour.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

